{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>כִּי עַל כֵּן עֲבַרְתֶּם</b> (for since you have passed by): since your way has brought you to me, it is not right that you not rest a little with me. <b>כֵּן תַּעֲשֶׂה כַּאֲשֶׁר דִּבַּרְתָּ</b> (so shall you do as you have spoken) — this is the way of rebuke, that bread suffices; this is the language of Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 18:5). Or he says: so shall you do for us — to lean under the tree and to be on your way immediately, for we are emissaries, and do not delay us to come into the tent or to lodge with you."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra reads the verse as Abraham speaking; the alternative reading attributes the words כֵּן תַּעֲשֶׂה to the visitors. Ramban reports both without explicit endorsement."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:30:45.735201628Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}